"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th. The project has successfully completed its testing and design phases, with a prototype for secure file sharing tested ahead of schedule. Omar Jensen is leading the development phase, which began next month. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption, effective January next year. A partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology is being explored. The budget was initially $500,000, adjusted to $550,000, and later approved at $2M by the executive board to cover all phases. A milestone celebration is scheduled for October 10th, and budget allocations will be discussed on August 1st."
